Z||000008||VISCERAL||04-23-2000||10:06 PM||||It's a friend's car. They're are mas mgr from discount tire. they're 18x7.5 all around. 225/40/18's all around. he's got coilovers in the back, so he has room. I believe the rims are 40 mm offset. I might get them in a 17" myself. but I think there wouldn't be much difference in ride between 45 or 40 series tires, so 17" or 18" is negligible. I would worry about potholes though.||||reg||1
Z||000009||TwisT||04-24-2000||09:29 AM||||VISC,  what is your friend running for suspension in the front?||||reg||1
Z||000010||VISCERAL||04-24-2000||10:03 AM||||Eibachs in the front. Coilovers in the rear.<BR>Kyb's all around. Mine is also this low but I have st springs in the front and coilovers in the rear, along with a strut tower brace bar, w/konis all around. If your'e gonna do lowering springs go w/eibachs. the Suspension Technique springs are too stiff, makes my car a little bouncy. I gonna put the battery in the front to add some weight, then play w/the konis. Gonna get the $45.00 front battery tray from V8Archie and some 9 foot battery cables from my local parts store, biggest guage possible and they're like $8 each. I need to ask him how to clamp up the cables. I think i'm gonna use a garden hose to cover the cables. ||||reg||10
Z||000011||1FST2M6||04-24-2000||10:45 AM||||absolutley beautiful! LOVE IT!   what offset? ||||reg||1
Z||000012||VISCERAL||04-24-2000||11:24 AM||||I believe they are 40 mm offset, check the discounttire.com site to be 100% sure.||||reg||1
Z||000013||batboy||04-24-2000||11:16 PM||||Looks like most of the younger dudes like it. Maybe I'm too old, but there's too much wheel and not enough tire. Personally, I think 16" wheels are about ideal.||||reg||1
Z||000014||WKDFIRO||04-25-2000||05:32 AM||||I would have to agree. I have 16s and I love them with 225/50. They have just enough meat to look buff. Also, I don't care for wheels that have no depth to them. Give me a rim that has a lip to polish and isn't flat with the tire. Thats what I like about the muscle cars wheels. I have seen and like some 17 inch wheels but they start to really make the rotors and calipers (stock) look tiny. Give me 16s and I'll go faster than a 17 or 18 inch wheel. Why? Cuz I can go as fast as I want and not have to worry about destroying my wheels on a pothole!||||reg||6
Z||000015||TwisT||04-25-2000||09:39 AM||||Musclecars:  15" minimum,  my preference being skinnies in the front and fender-tucked meats in the back.<P>Sportscars:  (Fiero) 17" minimum.  Heh he.  Fieros are designed to HANDLE,  which plus-sizing enhances.  Give me a set of 18's...  today's tires have reinforced sidewalls,  which take the worry out of denting rims.<P>To each his own (young AND old!).  lol||||reg||1
Z||000016||Raydar||04-25-2000||09:23 PM||||WKD... Agree with you completely. Always liked a deeper dish wheel. 16's with 45's-50's are big enough to suit my taste, especially on a car the size of the Fiero. <P>But... To each, his (or her) own. <BR>(Wouldn't it be boring if everybody liked the same thing?)  <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-25-2000).]||||reg||1
